A lineage whose own joinSchema refers to another package of its module,
narrowed where package fleet uses it. The narrowing admits references out of
the lineage only in what it unifies in; the joinSchema the lineage writes is
refused as it is unnarrowed (ref-import), along every narrowed path.
-- normal.cue --
import "example.com/fleet/common"

name: "ship"
joinSchema: common.#Headers
schemas: "0": "0": schema: {authorization?: =~"^Bearer "}
-- narrowing.cue --
{joinSchema: {"content-type"?: "application/json", ...}}
-- common/common.cue --
package common

#Headers: {[=~"^[a-z-]+$"]: string, ...}
-- out/verdict --
# bind
E0143 joinSchema refers to #Headers, in package "example.com/fleet/common", which is not one of CUE's builtin packages
# ids
0.0 g2.d3ff708ffd872f1fe5e3d5036a37963e17298b75a38e479232127a2a968bf312:g2.44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a
